WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:09.050
I've got my practice kit, underwear, 
socks, toiletries, rule book,

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.890
secret notebook, and snacks for the bus.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.510
Okay, that's everything.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.960
I'm so excited, I can't relax.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.140
<i>Today, we'll be featuring popular vacation 
destinations we recommend you visit.</i>

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.300
<i>How do you two spend your time off?</i>

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.850
<i>He eats parfaits at a dog café
with his chihuahua.</i>

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.100
<i>Can you believe it? And that's not all...</i>

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.220
Yes? Hello?

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.690
<i>Tree Trunk! Are you still asleep?!</i>

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.550
G-Gion-kun?

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:58.200
<b>I'm going shopping
 with your dad. 

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.490
<i>Have you finished packing 
for the training camp?</i>

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.200
What? Doesn't it start tomorrow?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.750
And I thought we didn't have practice today...

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.460
<i>I'm already packed.</i>

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.130
<i>I'm antsy now I've got nothing else to do,
so come practice with me right now.</i>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.110
What?

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:09.480
<i>We'll meet at the station.</i>

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.000
H-Hey, wait...

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.970
Hello?

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.470
It's way cheaper doing this 
than shopping in Sugadaira.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:09.180
<b>Episode 16 
You've Prepared</b>

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:08.850
Isn't it just?

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.690
Rie-chin, you're a smart shopper.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.140
But these bags are heavy.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:15.790
We should've brought some 
of the boys with us to carry them.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.880
That'd be putting their muscles to good use.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.090
But they have a rest day 
before the training camp.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.140
We should let them relax.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.980
Umenon, you're too nice.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.850
What's wrong, Umenon?

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.150
It's our captain and vice-captain...

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:54.670
Sekizan, you're not buying 
them for yourself...

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.380
Y-Yeah.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.750
Should I get strawberry or mango?

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.600
No, maybe Japanese sweets would be better.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:07.410
I think he'd prefer crackers over sweets.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.710
Are they shopping for the training camp?

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.480
Department store sweets at a training camp?

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.400
No way.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.480
Yeah, you're right.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.820
Which means...

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.610
Which means...

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.070
They're shopping for presents 
for their girlfriends!

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:26.830
"This is for you."

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.450
<b>This is 
for you</b>

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.450
There's no way that would happen!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.710
What are you guys doing?

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.600
Oh, you're Keijo's manager.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.160
H-Hello...

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.370
You're going to Coach Komori's house?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.900
Yeah, for a pre-training camp meeting.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.630
So you were shopping for 
something to bring with you.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.390
Yeah.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.640
He invited us to meet him for lunch,

00:04:55.050 --> 00:05:00.600
but I thought it would be 
polite to bring something.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.900
What?!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.150
You're having lunch at the old man's house?!

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.550
What the hell? That's not fair.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.700
I want lunch, too.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.160
Gion-kun, you should show some restraint.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.580
But we just finished practicing. I'm hungry.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.550
You were practicing?

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:20.210
Yeah.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:23.840
Tree Trunk said we should rest up
 for the training camp,

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.210
so we read rugby books 
in the library instead.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.460
Good boy.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:35.250
Anyway, I'm hungry after using my brain.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.290
I'll go have lunch at the old man's place, too.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.590
I can't give you special treatment.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:43.570
It would set a bad example 
to the rest of the guys.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.060
Why not? Who cares?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.540
Sir.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.030
Don't be selfish.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.270
I'll treat you to something next time.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:58.170
Later. Don't be late tomorrow.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.790
Bye.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:04.920
Should we go get burgers or something, then?

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.660
No.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:16.130
I'm hungry.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.940
You don't usually practice on 
your own, Sumiyoshi-senpai.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.580
Shut up.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.400
And Noka-senpai's not with you, either.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:29.300
I invited him, but he said he wanted
to rest because he overdid it

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.440
in morning practice yesterday.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:36.250
And what makes you think we do 
everything together, anyway?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.580
Boys.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.830
Don't forget to lock up.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:40.600
Yes, sir.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.300
Thanks for practicing 
with us, Yoshida-sensei.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.710
Hello?

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.270
Sure.

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:49.470
Make sure you head straight home.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.970
What? <i>Of course</i> we'll be there!

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:59.520
I studied so hard, I'm exhausted!

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:04.690
Why do I have to take extra classes 
the day before the training camp?

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.080
Takebe.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.570
Did you have class, too?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.450
You guys had class, too, huh?

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:12.320
Yeah.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.210
If you don't get your act together, 
you'll have to repeat the year.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:17.830
I know!

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.330
I'll tutor you.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.710
N-No, thanks. I'll be fine.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.890
Don't be shy.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:28.170
We may be stupid, but we can at 
least handle second-year problems.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:42.900
Kasuga, you tutor him.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.310
You're the one who offered. 
Don't make me do it.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:48.610
You're three ranks above me in our grade!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.570
I'm at 212, and you're at 207!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.120
That's four, not three!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.130
You can't even do basic subtraction?

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.890
<b>It's five...</b>

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.890
I-I'll be fine, really.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:03.050
Maroudo's finding someone to tutor us.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.210
See? That's him right now.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.460
Gion Kenji

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.460
What? Gion?

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.830
Sorry.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.750
So that's what you're into?

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.450
W-Well, you're...

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.490
It's that stupid little punk.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:38.570
<i>You need to cover up, my long-haired beauty.</i>

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:48.710
Hello?

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.960
<b>Ramen 
Kisuke</b>

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:50.960
What? Now?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.470
O-Okay...

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.340
What should we do?

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:01.800
We got triple helpings and 
ten orders of potstickers.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.900
There's no turning back now!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.310
We'll go after we eat!

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:11.410
Shall we?

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.320
Yeah.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.460
Thanks for the food.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:21.330
<b>Special offers every Sunday</b>

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.560
Here's your four plates of fried rice
on the house.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:19.940
Atsuta, you bastard!

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.330
What are you doing?!

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.320
Okay, that's everyone.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.460
Um...

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.560
We haven't gotten in touch 
with Oharano-kun yet.

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:31.340
What?!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:36.720
H-He's not answering his cell,
and his brother answered his home phone.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:41.050
He said he was walking their dog.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.850
We're going over there.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:44.840
What?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.830
What's wrong? Are you tired already?

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.860
You're hopeless.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.010
There, there.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.150
There he is.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.540
Gion.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:01.620
I'm glad we found you.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.470
And I thought you were supposed 
to be <i>walking </i>your dog...

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.010
Why are you carrying him?

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.490
It's fine.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.580
Pomekichi gets tired easily.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.500
"Pomekichi"?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.750
That's his name.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.760
Anyway, what do you want?

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.490
Oh, right.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:22.390
We're all going to eat 
lunch at Komori's place.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:25.350
Really? Say "hi" to the guys for me, then.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.770
Hey, wait.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:31.480
The captain said he won't 
take us unless everyone goes.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:34.610
So you should come with us.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.360
Why do I have to go?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.360
To eat lunch, duh.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.480
I'm not hungry.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.910
Well, I am. So...

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.380
Hey, you have your phone with you!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:50.190
Why didn't you pick up when 
we called you earlier?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:50.870
Huh?

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.540
I couldn't be bothered.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.220
You bastard!

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:00.180
Let go of me! Hey, you!

00:10:56.350 --> 00:11:00.180
Anyway, what are you doing here, Gion-kun?

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.300
<b>Tatsu-chan
I showed some Jinko guys your route. 
Did they find you?</b>

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:02.680
Oh.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.190
Sheesh.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.440
<b>Komori</b>

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.190
We made it!

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:25.030
Hey! It's time for lunch!

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.660
I brought everyone.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.460
Now it doesn't count as 
"special treatment," right?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.010
Hamburgers...

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.010
Okay!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.640
What's going on?

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.200
We're all having lunch at your place!

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.980
Yeah!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.130
I'm sorry.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.650
Gion overheard us.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:04.060
I can't feed all of you. Go—

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:13.540
It looks like the entire team's shown up.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.850
I'm sending them home right—

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.760
I'll go buy 20 cups!

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:22.440
Yumi!

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.180
Don't worry about us!

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:34.690
My, my, my...

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.190
Excuse the intrusion!

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.690
Nice to meet you!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.310
There are so many young men here.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:42.010
What are we going to do, darling?

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.200
Who cares?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.090
I'm really sorry about this.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.530
Oh, my. Your hair is incredible.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:50.980
I'm Sekizan, the captain.

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:54.240
Uh, what should I call you?

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.030
What?

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.440
Yumi-chan!

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:02.590
Don't be ridiculous, you idiot!

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:09.620
We all pitched in and bought meat and 
vegetables at the nearby supermarket.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.600
Could we borrow something to cook with?

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:12.890
The hotplate.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.830
Darling, it should be upstairs.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:15.780
Go get it.

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:16.980
What?

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.440
We'll get it...

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.460
It's fine. You're our guests.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.430
Darling, go.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:24.260
That thing is huge.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.380
Hey, you. Come help me.

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.620
What? Okay.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.950
You're all so big...

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.490
A child ought to be more like you. So cute.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:40.840
We don't have any kids.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:50.890
Yeah, but if you did have kids, 
they'd look more like that.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.090
I'm Yoshida, their advisor.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.150
She looks really unhappy.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.380
Put it outside.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.480
Is this enough sauce?

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:16.040
You boil corn, right?

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.500
You idiot!

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:20.920
You grill corn with the leaves on!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.000
Hirota?

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:26.020
Watch the flames!

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:26.950
O-Okay!

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:32.010
Don't! That meat needs 20 more seconds!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.510
Okay, sorry!

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.850
He's so anal.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:41.270
Nineteen, eighteen, seventeen, 
sixteen, fifteen...

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.750
And he's drooling more than anyone else.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:45.530
Don't blow bubbles while we're cooking!

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.520
Atsuta, you need more training!

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.870
Five years of prep, eight years of grilling!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.570
Yes, master!

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.350
He's been grilling for twelve years?

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.890
Fourteen, you mean.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.460
It's actually thirteen.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:03.540
I'm cooking rice, but will I have enough?

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:05.500
There's not enough to go round, is there?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.840
We bought a bunch of microwaveables, too.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:12.240
And if that's still not enough, 
we can feed them cabbage.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.720
You're so dependable.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.830
Can I borrow your microwave?

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:18.850
Go right ahead.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.540
Feeding us cabbage?

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:21.520
Cabbage...

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.530
It's so good.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.910
Mutsumi-san, it's ready!

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:31.910
Thanks. You got permission 
to come today, huh?

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:35.780
Yeah.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.580
Hey, lackey. Grill me some meat, too.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.170
Shut up. Do it yourself.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:48.170
It's great, even after a 
triple helping of ramen.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.660
There's always room for meat.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.130
Put a triple helping of meat on.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.390
Yes, sir.

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.160
<b>Hiss</b>

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.160
<b>Ahhhhh</b>

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.730
A triple helping of cabbage, too.

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.110
Yes, sir.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.350
<b>Ooooh</b>

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.350
<b>Hiss</b>

00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:08.690
This cabbage is pretty good 
when you put salt on it.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.660
You're right. It's yummy.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.240
You guys will eat anything.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:21.040
Komori-san, I'm sorry.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.040
No matter how you look at it,
 this was a crazy idea.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:26.250
I should've stopped them.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.940
It's fine.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:36.260
I haven't seen my wife 
this excited for a while.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:39.180
Yumi-chan, could I have some rice?

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.390
Oh, my! I'll make it extra large for you!

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:46.020
I wasn't expecting you to come.

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:51.510
Well, actually, Gion dragged me here...

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.400
We have beer.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.410
Oh, I'm fine.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:17:00.500
Anyway, I should get going—

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.660
After you eat this!

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.580
This is for you two.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.720
Here, sir.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.590
Thanks for the food.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:21.760
W-We'll be playing a lot of 
games at Sugadaira, won't we?

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:22.720
Yeah.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:27.740
I'll be making them play every day.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:31.860
We should be pretty busy.

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:50.610
We emptied our purses buying this house,

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:54.880
but it looks so small with 
this many people in it.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:18:01.670
And with different thoughts 
and concerns on their minds,

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:06.380
all of these guys go charging into 
one another in pursuit of a single ball.

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:12.590
Of course, half-assing it 
won't unify them.

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:17.030
That's why we need so much preparation.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:20.280
Not just in mastering techniques,

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.660
but also learning to comprehend each other.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.160
To understand each other.

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:36.050
They say rugby games are decided 
before the game even starts.

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:40.800
Upsets are rare in rugby.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:50.310
The well-prepared team wins, 
and the unprepared team loses.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.380
Are you a losing team?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.440
No, sir!

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:07.950
Have you prepared yourselves to death?

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.460
Yes, sir!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.750
I puked during yesterday's practice!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.670
Hey, we're eating here!

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:17.370
That's right.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.920
You've prepared.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.100
You've laid the foundations.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:29.250
Starting tomorrow, you'll see 
for yourselves what works,

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.890
and what doesn't at Sugadaira.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:33.940
Got it?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.250
Yes, sir!

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:38.860
Let's eat!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:42.060
Darling, that was so cool.

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:42.950
Stop that.

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:46.300
Maybe I'll go to Sugadaira, too.

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.950
You don't need to come.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.730
Yumi-chan.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:50.860
Coming.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:53.390
Yoshida-sensei.

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:54.220
Yes?

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:58.640
There's a place I always go to get
 a drink when I go to Sugadaira.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.580
Should we drop in one night?

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:07.970
Yes, please.

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:12.730
You're all such good boys.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.460
Maybe I'll go to Sugadaira, after all.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.620
That's enough now.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:21.400
Yumi-chan, come with us!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:37.000
No! I want to go to Sugadaira!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.140
Don't be so selfish.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:41.860
There'd be nothing for you to do.

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:44.010
It'll also be hot and crowded.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:48.440
Anyway, I'm not sure there'd 
be anywhere for you to stay.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:51.620
<b>Hmph</b>

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:52.520
Men are always like that.

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:55.150
They're only concerned 
about their own enjoyment!

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.250
It's not like that.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:00.030
They always leave their women behind.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:03.890
Fine. I don't care what you do.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:04.780
Hey now...

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:08.420
You go ahead to Sugadaira 
or Brazil or wherever!

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:12.050
I'll stay at home forever...

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:20.300
<i>Let's take a closer look.</i>

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.330
<i>There it is!</i>

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:26.300
<i>A baby spotted seal.</i>

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:26.300
<b>Smile</b>

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:29.530
Oh, my! Oh, my! Oh my! What's this thing?

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:30.990
What <i>is</i> this, darling?

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:34.330
It's so, so, so, so cute!

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.980
Just look at it, darling! It's so cute!

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:42.270
It's so cute! Oh, it's so cute!

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.670
<i>She's got an easy life.</i>

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.820
<b>I'm excited for Sugadaira!</b>

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.820
<b>Miyuki-kun, does your training 
camp start tomorrow, too?</b>

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.820
<b>Yeah!</b>

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.820
<b>Did you finish packing?</b>

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.820
<b>Yeah, but I can't sleep.</b>

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.880
Leave it to me...

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:04.070
I'll take care of it...

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "Summer Training Camp"</b>

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.330
Next time: "Summer Training Camp."
